Third-party design provenance
=============================

The safety-pipeline DESIGN (trait seams InjectionScanner::scan_injection /
LeakScanner::scan_leaks, policy-engine shape, redaction approach) and the
sandbox/capability-lease designs in crates/gooseclaw-safety and
crates/gooseclaw-skills are DERIVED from study of:

    IronClaw — https://github.com/nearai/ironclaw
    License: MIT OR Apache-2.0
    Studied at commit b011eb3932a0e1ab8bbe833893599ca9ae4925c5 (tag ironclaw-v1.4.1, 2026-09-29)
    (sparse, read-only checkout under reference/ironclaw — not distributed)

No IronClaw source files are vendored as of Phase 1 (2026-10-27). Any future
vendoring (planned Phase 5) requires attribution headers, a supply-chain scan,
and explicit human go-ahead, per CLAUDE.md Tier 2.

GooseClaw drives Block's goose agent (https://github.com/block/goose,
Apache-2.0) over the Agent Client Protocol as a supervised subprocess; no
goose code is vendored.
